1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,800
Water quality monitoring should do more
than display numbers. It should help

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:08,000
operators detect problems and
respond before they escalate.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,714
Introducing DWMS. Sensor data, real-time
visualization, and a traceable response

4
00:00:13,714 --> 00:00:16,000
workflow in one platform.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:21,133
The hardware path supports pH,
total dissolved solids, and turbidity. These

6
00:00:21,133 --> 00:00:23,000
demonstration readings are simulated.

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Abnormal readings create alerts, showing
the affected parameter and condition.

8
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:33,783
DWMS connects detection with action,
requesting a response through predefined

9
00:00:33,783 --> 00:00:39,522
operating rules. This pump activity is
a simulation; no physical equipment is

10
00:00:39,522 --> 00:00:40,000
connected.

11
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:48,250
Critical conditions latch emergency mode,
request a stop, and prevent automatic

12
00:00:48,250 --> 00:00:49,000
restart.

13
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:55,417
Returning readings alone cannot clear
the interlock. Recovery requires an operator

14
00:00:55,417 --> 00:00:56,000
acknowledgement.

15
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,111
Once readings recover, the operator
confirms recovery, allowing a controlled return

16
00:01:02,111 --> 00:01:06,000
to normal operation
and recording the transition.

17
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:11,714
Historical trends, device records, and
site grouping provide operational visibility

18
00:01:11,714 --> 00:01:17,429
across monitoring locations. The software
integration is tested with isolated

19
00:01:17,429 --> 00:01:18,000
fixtures.

20
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:22,190
Ethm is designed to explain
authorized monitoring evidence. Live AI remains

21
00:01:22,190 --> 00:01:26,000
unavailable until provider credit is
restored. AI never controls equipment.

22
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:32,750
DWMS. Turning water data into
accountable decisions. Monitor. Detect. Respond.

23
00:01:32,750 --> 00:01:36,000
Ahmed Alzahrani. Founder and Project Lead.
